 "notes": [
  "THE HONOUR ARENA -- the Attack tab's ARENA body (client/scenes/attack/arena_view.gd), cut from arena.png (art/slices/arena.json).",
  "arena.png paints its own header and its own four-tab band, and attack.png's are canonical: the strip stays where client/layout/attack.json puts it and this body is laid 130 units HIGHER than painted -- arena.png's tab rule stands at 483, attack.png's at 353. Every rect here is the painting's y less 130, which puts the league card's top at 362, one unit above attack.png's own first card at 364. The chests.png precedent, and it means a shift that reads wrong is one number here rather than a re-cut.",
  "league_emblem: the live league's arma (arena/league_<id>, cut from arena_kit.png at 277..304 wide) drawn DOWN into the painted crest's own 248-wide box, which covers the painted lion exactly -- the rule attack.json uses for a rival's portrait.",
  "bar_track / bar_fill: the painted channel with its gold lifted, and a stretch of that gold drawn along its inside to the lord's rating. The fraction is the SERVER'S (bar_from, bar_to, rating): the client places the fill, it never works out a league threshold.",
  "ticket: five pips at the painting's own pitch of 63, each drawn lit or spent from its own crop.",
  "rival: one card, flowed as many times as the server sends. Its portrait sits over the painted one; its crest, name, level and might are the server's."
 ],
